+# taffy (machopo's fork)
+
+| | |
+| --- | --- |
+| Upstream | https://github.com/DioxusLabs/taffy (fetched by URL; no remote) |
+| Fork | https://github.com/wusyong/taffy (remote `origin`) |
+| Branch | `machopo`, from upstream's `main` at `4aca4f4933` (2026-11-06); the fork's `main` is upstream's, untouched |
+| Version | 0.15.0 in `Cargo.toml`: v0.15.1's changes and the unreleased ones after it |
+| License | MIT (`LICENSE`) |
+| Used by | machopo's `crates/layout` (block, flexbox and grid layout, through taffy's low-level traits on machopo's own box tree), by path |
+
+## Why a fork
+
+machopo follows upstream's main rather than its releases: upstream keeps
+fixing what a browser runs into (floats, baselines, `aspect-ratio`), and
+waiting for a release left machopo working around them or listing them as
+known limitations. A change machopo needs is made here as a commit that can
+go upstream as it is; it stays in the fork only until upstream has it, or,
+when upstream won't take it, with the reason in the table below.
+
+The branch first started at the tag machopo used from crates.io (`v0.15.0`;
+the tag `machopo-2026-11-10` is that branch's tip), so that moving to the
+fork changed nothing.
+
+## Local modifications
+
+The commits on `machopo` after upstream's, each a patch in machopo's
+`patches/taffy/` (`python3 scripts/ci.py patches taffy` exports them;
+`python3 scripts/ci.py third-party` checks that they give this branch):
+
+| Commit | What | Upstream |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| Don't measure the items' heights for the width of a single-line column | A column flex container that is only asked for its width takes the largest of its items' hypothetical outer widths, each measured at the height its own style gives it, without measuring their heights first: one line breaking less of every paragraph in it. An item whose width follows the height it is given other than through `aspect-ratio` (a measure function's own, a column that wraps) gets the width of its style's height, not of the height it flexes to. Tests: `tests/hand_written/column_width.rs` and the measure count in `caching.rs`. | Drafted, not sent |
+| Add README.machopo.md | This file. Always the last commit, and the only one that changes it, so that the others can go upstream as they are. | Fork only |
+
+Changes are marked with `machopo:` comments. A change meant for upstream
+keeps taffy's `rust-version` (1.71), checked with that toolchain before it
+is sent; the fork itself builds with machopo's pinned toolchain (taffy pins
+none). Anything sent upstream is drafted first and reviewed before it goes
+out.
+
+## Tests
+
+```sh
+cargo test                       # taffy's own, in this checkout
+```
+
+and, in machopo, `cargo test -p layout` and the reftests and WPT of what
+the change touches.
+
+## Updating
+
+1. Fetch upstream by URL (`git fetch https://github.com/DioxusLabs/taffy
+   main`) and rebase `machopo` onto the new upstream commit, fixing any
+   conflicts. Drop the commits upstream now has; keep this file's commit
+   last.
+2. Update the start and version above, and the table.
+3. Push `machopo` (`--force-with-lease`); first tag the old tip
+   (`machopo-<date>`) so that machopo's older pins can still be fetched.
+4. In machopo: `third_party.toml`'s `rev` and `upstream_rev`, then
+   `python3 scripts/ci.py patches taffy`, then `cargo test --workspace`,
+   the reftests and WPT. Upstream's API changes show up as build errors in
+   `crates/layout`.
